13.4 Ergodicity Assumption
The proof sketch assumes ergodic or mixing dynamics. For non-ergodic systems (attractor confinement), the proposition applies only within accessible subsets.

13.5 Finite Dimensionality
The proposition assumes 
d
<
∞
d<∞. Extension to effectively infinite-dimensional systems (e.g., Phase 12 PIRL) requires separate analysis.

14. THEORETICAL IMPLICATIONS
14.1 What Phase 10.5 Established
Claim	Evidence	Strength
Coverage and novelty are negatively correlated	r = -0.513, power = 85.2%	Moderate
Occupancy stabilizes before full coverage	Cov ≈ 0.61-0.62 across all horizons	Strong
Novelty exhibits phase structure	Expansion → Peak → Compression	Strong
Effective dimensionality is lower than nominal	d_eff = 9 (nominal 16)	Moderate
Systems revisit previously occupied regions	Revisit rate = 1.0	Strong
14.2 What Phase 10.5 Did NOT Establish
Universal saturation law

Statistical significance at p < 0.05

Asymptotic convergence proof

Causal relationship between occupancy and novelty

Ground truth coverage measurement

14.3 The New Research Identity of OCES
After Phase 10.5, OCES is now best interpreted as:

An exploratory geometric-operational framework studying occupancy-driven exploratory compression in recursively self-modeling inferential systems under bounded representational dynamics.

This is significantly stronger than:

"Conscious AI"

"Synthetic awareness"

"Recursive sentience"

